coder › Changed CSV formula-injection handling and added tests on branch `fix-csv-injection`.

What changed:
- `src/csv.ts` — `field()` now branches on `typeof cell === 'number'` and writes numbers plainly via `String(cell)`, so `-1` stays `-1`. String fields starting with `=`, `+`, `-`, `@`, tab, or carriage return are written as `"'<text>"` (single quote prefixed, whole field double-quoted, inner `"` doubled). All other strings keep the existing `,",\n` quoting with `"` doubling.
- `src/csv.test.ts` — kept the comma test; added tests for `=HYPERLINK(...)` (incl. inner-quote doubling), `+`, `-`, `@`, tab, `\r` prefixing; plain negative/decimal numbers; preserved comma/quote/newline quoting.

Decisions not in the request: detected numbers by `typeof` (not by regex on text), so numeric `-1` is plain while string `"-1"` is escaped; the injection branch always quotes and doubles inner quotes even when the field has no comma/quote/newline.

